--- !u!1001 &7431893767880468293
PrefabInstance:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  serializedVersion: 2
  m_Modification:
    serializedVersion: 3
    m_TransformParent: {fileID: 1702387512758425278}
    m_Modifications:
    - target: {fileID: 2116517601969916342, guid: 183e809bca3827e41a67b7345a91f0c2, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_text
      value: 'The increasing acceptance of video games in the mainstream combined
        with new technological innovations led to the golden age of arcade games,
        occurring from 1979 to 1983.


        As a result of the arcade game boom,
        machines would push their processing units to innovate their graphics. Notable
        developments include using colour palettes instead of just black and white,
        vector rendering, and early iterations of 2.5D graphics.


        The golden
        age of arcade games would gradually wear down around 1982, ending with the
        video game crash of 1983 as a result of oversaturation and lack of quality
        in business practices.

'
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 2116517601969916342, guid: 183e809bca3827e41a67b7345a91f0c2, type: 3}
